{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 104, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When the direct input-to-output edge is missing, a skip on edge 4 supplies a needed residual path, giving much larger gains than when edge 3 already carries an op."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing an existing skip shortcut on edge 3 with a conv removes the residual path and hurts, whereas filling an empty edge 3 gives large gains."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "In conv-heavy cells the edge-3 shortcut is essential for trainability, so removing it costs much more than in pool- or skip-dominated cells, where removal can even help."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without edge 3, edge 5 is one of few remaining paths to the output, so deleting it is far more damaging."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv to an empty edge 1 adds capacity and a path, while replacing a skip there loses a useful identity path."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Pooling on an empty edge 1 adds a path at little cost, whereas overwriting a conv or skip with pooling removes useful computation."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "In pool-dominated cells that lack any conv, adding a 3x3 conv supplies the cell's only learnable feature extraction and gives large gains."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Overwriting a 3x3 conv on edge 4 with a skip removes learnable capacity, which is catastrophic in cells where it is the only conv."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input-to-output residual where none exists greatly improves optimization, more than swapping an existing op on edge 3 for a skip."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "When other edges carry skips instead of convs, the cell lacks learnable operations, so adding a 3x3 conv on edge 0 yields much larger gains."}], "tok": 33946, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor